From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Verrilli <mverrilli@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 21:53:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add CUDA kernels and ops for TurboQuant KV compression

Adds the GGML_OP_TQ_* op family backing TurboQuant KV-cache compression
(arXiv:2504.19874), with reference implementations on CPU and CUDA.

Ops:
  GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE          per-head scalar-quantize K with optional
                             rotation, outlier split, asymmetric mean
  GGML_OP_TQ_DEQUANT         expand packed K back to f16 (with optional
                             fused Walsh-Hadamard undo)
  GGML_OP_TQ_DEQUANT_KV      combined K+V dequant in a single graph node
  GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE_V        per-head scalar-quantize V
  GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE_KV       combined K+V encode in a single graph node
  GGML_OP_TQ_FLASH_ATTN_EXT  fused inline-decode flash attention against
                             packed K (+ optionally packed V)
  GGML_OP_TQ_WHT             standalone Walsh-Hadamard rotation

Addressing model. Each op takes an optional locs source tensor: when
non-null, dense token i maps to physical cache slot locs[i] (indexed mode
used by sliding-window caches whose eviction fragments free cells);
otherwise cells are sequential starting at firstCell (contiguous fast
path used by plain Causal caches). The kernel branches block-uniformly
on the locs pointer, so the contiguous case carries no per-iteration cost.

CUDA backend ships per-D fused flash-attention TUs for D in {64, 128,
256, 512} covering llama, qwen and gemma head dims. The encoder uses a
biased codebook-aware scale refinement (RaBitQ-style; arXiv:2604.18555)
selected adaptively against the RMS estimator. Pascal cc 6.x and AMD
RDNA3 each get their own per-arch tuning in tq-fattn-vec.cuh.
